diff --git a/docs/album-photo-context-menu.md b/docs/album-photo-context-menu.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..26c42e6963
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/album-photo-context-menu.md
@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@
+# Per-photo interaction in an album
+
+Long-pressing a photo of an album does not act on the whole message any more. It acts on that one photo, and the finger can move
+to another photo without being lifted. The editing of the album is in [album-photo-editing.md](album-photo-editing.md).
+
+Code: `ChatAlbumPhotoContextMenu.swift` (menu items, tracking, swiping), `ChatAlbumPhotoContextSource.swift` (the selection and the
+card), `ChatControllerOpenMessageContextMenu.swift` (where the menu is made), and, for the finger-driven scrolling, `ContextUI` /
+`ContextControllerImpl`.
+
+## The modes
+
+| Mode | How it starts | What the finger does |
+|---|---|---|
+| Photo menu on the lifted album | long press on a photo | The whole album is lifted, one photo is active ("Photo 6 of 10"). Moving over another photo makes that one active and rebuilds the menu. |
+| Card of one photo | the finger stays still on a photo for a while | The album turns into one photo on a card in the middle of the screen. The finger goes up and down with a limit and settles back when lifted; a move of 70 pt up or down goes to the next or previous photo, 40 pt sideways does the same. |
+| Menu of the whole album | "Whole Album" in the photo menu, or a long press that is not on a photo (for example on the caption) | The usual menu of the message, with Edit Album in place of Edit. Reply comes first, then Edit Album. |
+
+## The menu of one photo
+
+Reply (the reply panel says which photo, "Photo 4 of 9", and shows its thumbnail), Edit Photo, Add to Saved, Forward, Delete, Select,
+Whole Album. The items that depend on rules of the regular menu (who can reply, forward or delete, copy protection) are taken from the
+regular menu of that one message, so the rules stay in one place.
+
+- **Edit Photo** is the ordinary edit of the message of that photo: the edit panel says "Edit Photo" and "Photo N of M", with the
+  thumbnail on the left. The thumbnail follows the photo when it is replaced.
+- **Add to Saved** forwards that photo alone, with no text, to Saved Messages, and shows the usual notice.
+
+## Reactions
+
+Reactions belong to the album as a whole.
+
+- The menu of one photo has none, on the lifted album and on the card, so that moving over the photos changes nothing above the content.
+- The menu of the whole album has them, including the one that opens from "Whole Album". They are not known when the photo menu is
+  made, so a box (`AlbumReactionsBox`) is filled when they are, and the "Whole Album" menu reads it. The items of that menu need
+  `context` and `animationCache` set, or the engine silently shows no reactions.
+
+## Moving over a tall album
+
+An album of many tall photos does not fit on the screen, so photos are out of reach of the finger. The engine scrolls lifted content
+together with the menu, and the finger would normally drag it. That is the wrong thing while choosing a photo, so while the finger is
+down on the photos of the lifted album the scrolling is driven by the finger the other way round:
+
+- A finger that goes up brings the photos above it down to it; a finger that goes down brings the ones below up.
+- The distance is the distance of the finger times `albumScrollFactor` (0.6; 1.0 is the same distance). This is the number to tune.
+- The album never goes past either end, with no bounce, so a finger that goes down over the top of the album does not pull it down.
+- This applies only to a finger that is down on the photos of the lifted album. A touch that starts anywhere else (the menu, the
+  rest of the screen) scrolls as usual, and so does everything in the actions of the whole album, on the card, and with no finger down.
+- The finger that opened the menu moves the album from its own position updates. Every other finger is followed by a small
+  recognizer (`AlbumPhotoScrollDriver`) that sees every touch from its start to its end and takes none of them. Only while a touch
+  that began on a photo is down is the usual scrolling switched off, and it is given back the moment that touch ends or is cancelled.
+  The scrolling is therefore never left off by a missed "finger lifted" event, which an earlier version did (a finger that moved
+  at once never produced one), and the clock re-applies the state every 0.1 s as a safety net.
+- A finger that goes from the photos onto the menu highlights the item under it, and lifting it there runs the item. This is done
+  explicitly, for the finger that opened the menu and for the others (`highlightMenu(atWindowPoint:)` and `finishMenuHighlight`),
+  because the engine's own handling for the finger that opened the menu did not work every time here. Going back over the photos
+  takes the highlight away.
+- Menu selection is on for the whole mode: a touch that begins on a menu item slides over the menu to choose an item, as in any menu
+  (also when the content is taller than the screen, where the engine would otherwise switch that off); a touch that begins anywhere
+  else is not taken by it and scrolls.
+
+### Engine API this needed
+
+Four methods on `ContextController`, carried through `ContextControllerImpl` to `ContextControllerExtractedPresentationNode`
+(other presentation nodes get a no-op default):
+
+- `setContentScrollingDriven(_ isDriven: Bool, menuSelection: Bool)`: with `isDriven` the finger no longer scrolls the lifted
+  content; with `menuSelection` a finger that is down can slide over the menu even if the content is taller than the screen.
+- `scrollContent(by:)`: moves the content by a distance (positive moves it up), clamped to both ends, no bounce.
+- `highlightMenu(atWindowPoint:)` and `finishMenuHighlight(performAction:)`: highlight the menu item under a window point (nothing
+  for nil), and run the highlighted item or only drop the highlight.
+
+A touch that is already down when the scroller is switched off or on is not affected by it (a scroller starts only from a new
+touch), which is why the state is decided at the start of a touch.
+
+## Things that are easy to get wrong
+
+- Never keep "scrolling is off" as a flag that is cleared by a "finger lifted" event. Derive it from the touches that are down
+  (see `AlbumPhotoScrollDriver`); events such as the end of a press are not delivered for every touch.
+- The menu moves when its height changes (the content and the menu are fitted together on the screen), so rebuilding it per photo
+  can move the message. This is the reason reactions were removed from the per-photo menu.
+- The `Edit Photo` and `Add to Saved` icons: the bookmark picture is 30 pt, the other menu pictures 24 pt, so it is redrawn at 24.
diff --git a/docs/album-photo-editing.md b/docs/album-photo-editing.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..0c6e06c365
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/album-photo-editing.md
@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# Editing a photo album in a chat
+
+Long-pressing an album offers **Edit Album**: a window with the album's photos (the same list the paste preview uses), where the
+user can untick photos, add photos from the gallery, change their order, edit the caption and move it above or below the pictures.
+When the window is folded away, the pending changes wait in a bar that replaces the input panel (`AlbumEditInputPanelNode`) until they
+are saved or thrown away.
+
+The menu of one photo, its modes and the finger-driven scrolling are in [album-photo-context-menu.md](album-photo-context-menu.md).
+
+Code: `ChatAlbumPhotoContextMenu.swift` (`openAlbumEditor`, `applyAlbumEdit`), `AlbumEditSession.swift`,
+`AlbumEditInputPanelNode.swift`.
+
+## What the server allows today
+
+An album is a set of ordinary messages that share a `grouped_id`. The position of a photo is the order of its message. The API gives no
+way to:
+
+- add a message to an album that is already sent (a `grouped_id` is only created by one `sendMultiMedia` call),
+- move a message inside an album,
+- change the whole album in one step.
+
+What it does allow: delete a message of the album, edit one message (its media and its text), and send a new album.
+
+## The approach: fixed places
+
+An album keeps the places it had. The window never lets it grow:
+
+- The text over the album reads "Up to N photos - remove one to add another" while every place is taken, and "K photos can be added"
+  while K places are free (a photo was taken away).
+- The attachment button next to the caption field is hidden by default. It comes out from under the field when a photo is taken away
+  (unticked), and goes back under it when there is no free place.
+- What is added from the gallery goes only into the free places (the gallery button reads that the maximum is reached when more is
+  chosen than there are free places).
+
+`applyAlbumEdit` turns what the user left in the window into the smallest set of operations the server allows. The number of photos is
+never more than the number of messages, so the messages are always kept:
+
+- Messages whose photo is no longer wanted are deleted. Which ones are deleted is chosen by trying every choice and taking the one that
+  needs the fewest edits, so removing one photo from the middle without any other change is a single deletion.
+- A message that has to show another photo gets that photo through an edit of its media: a photo that was added is uploaded; a photo
+  that comes from another message of the album is sent as a copy of its local file (not by a reference to the other message, because
+  that message may be edited at the same moment and its photo may no longer be there when the reference is used).
+- Moving a photo is the same thing: the two messages involved are edited to show each other's photo.
+- The caption stays on the message that had it, or moves to the last remaining one. The caption position flag is written on every
+  message of the album.
+
+Because nothing is ever sent as a new album, reactions, replies and the position of the album in the history are kept.
+
+## Limits of this approach
+
+- A reorder or replacement is a set of independent media edits. Other users see the photos change one by one, not move.
+- Each edit is its own request. If one fails, the album is left half changed.
+- Photos that change places are uploaded again.
+- The album can never have more photos than it had; it can only shrink or have photos replaced.
+- At least one photo has to stay.
+- An audio file added in the window is not saved (photos and audio cannot be in one album).
+
+## What would make it better: server changes
+
+The workaround exists only because the album cannot be changed as one thing. With support on the server the whole thing becomes one
+atomic, cheap operation and the client logic above shrinks to a single call:
+
+- **Append to an album**: let `sendMedia` / `sendMultiMedia` take the `grouped_id` of an existing album (or add a dedicated method), so
+  new photos join the same album and the limit of fixed places goes away.
+- **Reorder**: a method that takes the album's message ids in their new order (or edits the album position of a message), so photos move
+  without being uploaded again.
+- **One call for the whole edit**: a method such as `messages.editMultiMedia` that takes the final list of media (existing ones by
+  id, new ones as uploads), the caption and its position, and applies it atomically to the group, with the result delivered to other
+  clients as a single update.
+- Keeping the identity of the messages (and so reactions, replies and the position in the history) when an album is changed.
+
+None of this exists in the current API, so it is a server-side change.
diff --git a/submodules/TelegramUI/Sources/AlbumEditInputPanelNode.swift b/submodules/TelegramUI/Sources/AlbumEditInputPanelNode.swift
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..30e29e1dc5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/submodules/TelegramUI/Sources/AlbumEditInputPanelNode.swift
@@ -0,0 +1,413 @@
+import Foundation
+import UIKit
+import AsyncDisplayKit
+import Display
+import TelegramCore
+import ChatPresentationInterfaceState
+import TelegramPresentationData
+import AppBundle
+import ChatInputPanelNode
+import GlassBackgroundComponent
+import ComponentFlow
+import ComponentDisplayAdapters
+import LottieComponent
+
+/// Three pictures that lie on one another, each a little to the right of and under the one before. Each has a gap round it where it lies
+/// on another one, which is cut out of that one, so the gap is the colour of what is behind the whole collage.
+///
+/// It starts level, every picture at the same height in the middle of the block, and half a second later settles into the staggered arrangement.
+private final class AlbumEditCollageView: UIView {
+    private final class DisplayLinkTarget {
+        var action: (() -> Void)?
+        @objc func fire() {
+            self.action?()
+        }
+    }
+    
+    private static let settleDelay: Double = 0.5
+    private static let settleDuration: Double = 0.4
+    
+    private var imageViews: [UIImageView] = []
+    private var images: [UIImage] = []
+    /// 0 is level, 1 is the final arrangement.
+    private var spread: CGFloat = 0.0
+    private var didScheduleSettle = false
+    private var displayLink: CADisplayLink?
+    private var settleStartTime: CFTimeInterval = 0.0
+    
+    deinit {
+        self.displayLink?.invalidate()
+    }
+    
+    func update(images: [UIImage]) {
+        self.images = images
+        self.layoutImages()
+        
+        if !self.didScheduleSettle && min(3, images.count) > 1 {
+            self.didScheduleSettle = true
+            DispatchQueue.main.asyncAfter(deadline: .now() + AlbumEditCollageView.settleDelay) { [weak self] in
+                self?.startSettling()
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    
+    private func startSettling() {
+        let target = DisplayLinkTarget()
+        target.action = { [weak self] in
+            self?.settleStep()
+        }
+        let displayLink = CADisplayLink(target: target, selector: #selector(DisplayLinkTarget.fire))
+        self.settleStartTime = CACurrentMediaTime()
+        displayLink.add(to: .main, forMode: .common)
+        self.displayLink = displayLink
+    }
+    
+    private func settleStep() {
+        let progress = min(1.0, (CACurrentMediaTime() - self.settleStartTime) / AlbumEditCollageView.settleDuration)
+        // Ease in and out.
+        self.spread = CGFloat(progress * progress * (3.0 - 2.0 * progress))
+        self.layoutImages()
+        if progress >= 1.0 {
+            self.displayLink?.invalidate()
+            self.displayLink = nil
+        }
+    }
+    
+    private func layoutImages() {
+        let images = self.images
+        let count = min(3, images.count)
+        while self.imageViews.count < count {
+            let imageView = UIImageView()
+            imageView.contentMode = .scaleAspectFill
+            imageView.clipsToBounds = true
+            imageView.layer.cornerRadius = 8.0
+            imageView.layer.cornerCurve = .continuous
+            self.addSubview(imageView)
+            self.imageViews.append(imageView)
+        }
+        while self.imageViews.count > count {
+            self.imageViews.removeLast().removeFromSuperview()
+        }
+        
+        let side: CGFloat = 28.0
+        let gap: CGFloat = 1.2
+        // Level, the pictures lie at the middle of the final arrangement (y = 4); the first one then rises and the last one sinks.
+        let offsets: [CGPoint] = [CGPoint(x: 0.0, y: 4.0 - 4.0 * self.spread), CGPoint(x: 6.0, y: 4.0), CGPoint(x: 12.0, y: 4.0 + 4.0 * self.spread)]
+        for index in 0 ..< count {
+            let imageView = self.imageViews[index]
+            imageView.image = images[index]
+            imageView.frame = CGRect(origin: offsets[index], size: CGSize(width: side, height: side))
+            
+            // The gaps are cut out with the same smoothed corners (continuous) the pictures have: a path with circular corners would not
+            // fit them. The corners are drawn by a layer, which is the one that knows that curve.
+            if index + 1 < count {
+                let bounds = imageView.bounds
+                let renderer = UIGraphicsImageRenderer(size: bounds.size)
+                let maskImage = renderer.image { rendererContext in
+                    let context = rendererContext.cgContext
+                    context.setFillColor(UIColor.black.cgColor)
+                    context.fill(bounds)
+                    context.setBlendMode(.destinationOut)
+                    for front in (index + 1) ..< count {
+                        let frontRect = CGRect(origin: CGPoint(x: offsets[front].x - offsets[index].x, y: offsets[front].y - offsets[index].y), size: CGSize(width: side, height: side)).insetBy(dx: -gap, dy: -gap)
+                        let cutout = CALayer()
+                        cutout.frame = CGRect(origin: CGPoint(), size: frontRect.size)
+                        cutout.backgroundColor = UIColor.black.cgColor
+                        cutout.cornerRadius = 8.0 + gap
+                        cutout.cornerCurve = .continuous
+                        context.saveGState()
+                        context.translateBy(x: frontRect.minX, y: frontRect.minY)
+                        cutout.render(in: context)
+                        context.restoreGState()
+                    }
+                }
+                let mask = CALayer()
+                mask.frame = bounds
+                mask.contents = maskImage.cgImage
+                mask.contentsScale = maskImage.scale
+                imageView.layer.mask = mask
+            } else {
+                imageView.layer.mask = nil
+            }
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/// The panel in the place of the input panel while the window that edits an album is folded away and there is something to save: the album
+/// (its first pictures and how many changes there are), its text, a button to throw the changes away and one to save them.
+final class AlbumEditInputPanelNode: ChatInputPanelNode, UITextViewDelegate {
+    private var session: AlbumEditSession
+    private var presentationInterfaceState: ChatPresentationInterfaceState?
+    
+    private let closeBackground = GlassBackgroundView(frame: CGRect())
+    private let closeIcon = UIImageView()
+    private let closeButton = HighlightTrackingButton()
+    
+    private let cardBackground = GlassBackgroundView(frame: CGRect())
+    private let lineView = UIImageView()
+    private let collageView = AlbumEditCollageView()
+    private let titleLabel = UILabel()
+    private let subtitleLabel = UILabel()
+    private let chevronView = UIImageView()
+    private let headerButton = HighlightTrackingButton()
+    private let textView = UITextView()
+    private let placeholderLabel = UILabel()
+    private let emojiView = ComponentHostView<Empty>()
+    private let applyBackground = UIView()
+    private let applyIcon = UIImageView()
+    private let applyButton = HighlightTrackingButton()
+    
+    init(session: AlbumEditSession) {
+        self.session = session
+        
+        super.init()
+        
+        self.closeIcon.contentMode = .center
+        self.closeBackground.contentView.addSubview(self.closeIcon)
+        self.closeButton.addTarget(self, action: #selector(self.closePressed), for: .touchUpInside)
+        self.view.addSubview(self.closeBackground)
+        
+        self.view.addSubview(self.cardBackground)
+        self.lineView.image = generateImage(CGSize(width: 2.0, height: 3.0), rotatedContext: { size, context in
+            context.clear(CGRect(origin: CGPoint(), size: size))
+            context.setFillColor(UIColor.black.cgColor)
+            context.addPath(UIBezierPath(roundedRect: CGRect(origin: CGPoint(), size: size), cornerRadius: 1.0).cgPath)
+            context.fillPath()
+        })?.withRenderingMode(.alwaysTemplate).stretchableImage(withLeftCapWidth: 0, topCapHeight: 1)
+        self.cardBackground.contentView.addSubview(self.lineView)
+        self.cardBackground.contentView.addSubview(self.collageView)
+        self.titleLabel.font = Font.medium(15.0)
+        self.cardBackground.contentView.addSubview(self.titleLabel)
+        self.subtitleLabel.font = Font.regular(14.0)
+        self.cardBackground.contentView.addSubview(self.subtitleLabel)
+        self.chevronView.contentMode = .center
+        self.cardBackground.contentView.addSubview(self.chevronView)
+        self.headerButton.addTarget(self, action: #selector(self.headerPressed), for: .touchUpInside)
+        
+        self.textView.backgroundColor = .clear
+        self.textView.textContainerInset = .zero
+        self.textView.textContainer.lineFragmentPadding = 0.0
+        self.textView.isScrollEnabled = false
+        self.textView.font = Font.regular(17.0)
+        self.textView.delegate = self
+        self.textView.attributedText = AlbumEditInputPanelNode.styledCaption(session.caption)
+        self.cardBackground.contentView.addSubview(self.textView)
+        self.placeholderLabel.font = Font.regular(17.0)
+        self.placeholderLabel.isUserInteractionEnabled = false
+        self.cardBackground.contentView.addSubview(self.placeholderLabel)
+        
+        self.emojiView.isUserInteractionEnabled = false
+        self.cardBackground.contentView.addSubview(self.emojiView)
+        self.applyIcon.contentMode = .center
+        self.applyBackground.addSubview(self.applyIcon)
+        self.applyButton.addTarget(self, action: #selector(self.applyPressed), for: .touchUpInside)
+        self.cardBackground.contentView.addSubview(self.applyBackground)
+        // The buttons are over the glass, in the panel itself: the glass takes no touches that start in it.
+        self.view.addSubview(self.closeButton)
+        self.view.addSubview(self.headerButton)
+        self.view.addSubview(self.applyButton)
+        
+        session.changed = { [weak self] in
+            self?.updateTexts()
+        }
+    }
+    
+    func updateSession(_ session: AlbumEditSession) {
+        if self.session !== session {
+            self.session = session
+            self.textView.attributedText = AlbumEditInputPanelNode.styledCaption(session.caption)
+            session.changed = { [weak self] in
+                self?.updateTexts()
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    
+    /// The text of the album as it is typed: 17 pt, with a line of 22 pt.
+    private static func styledCaption(_ caption: NSAttributedString) -> NSAttributedString {
+        let result = NSMutableAttributedString(attributedString: caption)
+        let style = NSMutableParagraphStyle()
+        style.minimumLineHeight = 20.0
+        style.maximumLineHeight = 20.0
+        let fullRange = NSRange(location: 0, length: result.length)
+        result.addAttribute(.paragraphStyle, value: style, range: fullRange)
+        result.enumerateAttribute(.font, in: fullRange, options: [], using: { value, range, _ in
+            if value == nil {
+                result.addAttribute(.font, value: Font.regular(17.0), range: range)
+            }
+        })
+        return result
+    }
+    
+    @objc private func closePressed() {
+        self.textView.resignFirstResponder()
+        self.session.discardRequested?()
+    }
+    
+    @objc private func headerPressed() {
+        self.textView.resignFirstResponder()
+        self.session.openRequested?()
+    }
+    
+    @objc private func applyPressed() {
+        self.textView.resignFirstResponder()
+        self.session.applyRequested?()
+    }
+    
+    func textViewDidChange(_ textView: UITextView) {
+        self.session.caption = textView.attributedText ?? NSAttributedString()
+        self.placeholderLabel.alpha = textView.text.isEmpty ? 1.0 : 0.0
+        self.updateTexts()
+    }
+    
+    /// The text typed in the window that was folded away is the text of the field. What is typed in the field itself is already in the session.
+    private func syncCaptionFromSession() {
+        if !self.textView.isFirstResponder && self.textView.attributedText?.string != self.session.caption.string {
+            self.textView.attributedText = AlbumEditInputPanelNode.styledCaption(self.session.caption)
+        }
+        self.placeholderLabel.alpha = self.textView.text.isEmpty ? 1.0 : 0.0
+    }
+    
+    /// The line under the name: how many changes there are.
+    private func updateTexts() {
+        guard let interfaceState = self.presentationInterfaceState else {
+            return
+        }
+        self.titleLabel.text = interfaceState.strings.Conversation_ContextMenuEditAlbum
+        self.subtitleLabel.text = interfaceState.strings.Conversation_AlbumEdit_UnsavedChanges(Int32(self.session.changeCount))
+    }
+    
+    override func updateLayout(width: CGFloat, leftInset: CGFloat, rightInset: CGFloat, bottomInset: CGFloat, additionalSideInsets: UIEdgeInsets, maxHeight: CGFloat, maxOverlayHeight: CGFloat, isSecondary: Bool, transition: ContainedViewLayoutTransition, interfaceState: ChatPresentationInterfaceState, metrics: LayoutMetrics, deviceMetrics: DeviceMetrics, isMediaInputExpanded: Bool) -> CGFloat {
+        self.presentationInterfaceState = interfaceState
+        let theme = interfaceState.theme
+        let isDark = theme.overallDarkAppearance
+        
+        // The margins of the input of the chat: 8 pt from the sides of the screen, and 18 pt more when the panel is over the rounded corners
+        // of the screen (there is no home indicator under it, which is when the keyboard is up).
+        let sideInset: CGFloat = 8.0
+        let compactSideInset = self.compactBottomSideInset(bottomInset: bottomInset, deviceMetrics: deviceMetrics)
+        let leftInset = leftInset + compactSideInset
+        let rightInset = rightInset + compactSideInset
+        let buttonSize: CGFloat = 40.0
+        
+        self.titleLabel.textColor = theme.chat.inputPanel.panelControlAccentColor
+        self.subtitleLabel.textColor = theme.chat.inputPanel.inputPlaceholderColor
+        self.placeholderLabel.text = interfaceState.strings.MediaPicker_AddCaption
+        self.placeholderLabel.textColor = theme.chat.inputPanel.inputPlaceholderColor
+        self.textView.textColor = theme.chat.inputPanel.inputTextColor
+        let typingStyle = NSMutableParagraphStyle()
+        typingStyle.minimumLineHeight = 20.0
+        typingStyle.maximumLineHeight = 20.0
+        self.textView.typingAttributes = [
+            .font: Font.regular(17.0),
+            .foregroundColor: theme.chat.inputPanel.inputTextColor,
+            .paragraphStyle: typingStyle
+        ]
+        self.syncCaptionFromSession()
+        self.placeholderLabel.alpha = self.textView.text.isEmpty ? 1.0 : 0.0
+        self.updateTexts()
+        self.collageView.update(images: self.session.collageImages)
+        
+        // The card is the one of the input with a reply: 8 pt from the sides of the screen, a header of 52 pt (where the reply has its line, here
+        // the first pictures of the album), and under it the row of the text, 40 pt when it is of one line, with the corners of the input.
+        let cardX = leftInset + sideInset + buttonSize + 6.0
+        let cardWidth = max(0.0, width - rightInset - sideInset - cardX)
+        let headerHeight: CGFloat = 52.0
+        let minimalRowHeight: CGFloat = 40.0
+        // The button that saves is as big as the send button of the input: 44 by 36. Before it, the icon of the emoji, as big as the icon of
+        // the stickers of the input (32 by 32).
+        let applySize = CGSize(width: 40.0, height: 34.0)
+        let emojiSize = CGSize(width: 32.0, height: 32.0)
+        let textWidth = max(0.0, cardWidth - 12.0 - 11.0 - emojiSize.width - 4.0 - applySize.width - 3.0)
+        let textHeight = ceil(min(110.0, max(20.0, self.textView.sizeThatFits(CGSize(width: textWidth, height: 10000.0)).height)))
+        // As in the input of the chat: the field is 31 pt at least, its text is at its top (5 pt under the header, the lines of 20 pt), and
+        // the row is the field and 9 pt.
+        let fieldHeight = max(31.0, textHeight + 11.0)
+        let rowHeight = max(minimalRowHeight, fieldHeight + 9.0)
+        let cardHeight = headerHeight + rowHeight
+        let cardFrame = CGRect(origin: CGPoint(x: cardX, y: 0.0), size: CGSize(width: cardWidth, height: cardHeight))
+        
+        transition.updateFrame(view: self.cardBackground, frame: cardFrame)
+        self.cardBackground.update(size: cardFrame.size, cornerRadius: floor(minimalRowHeight * 0.5), isDark: isDark, tintColor: .init(kind: .panel), isInteractive: false, transition: ComponentTransition(transition))
+        
+        // As in the reply: the title is at 10 pt, the line under it 1 pt below, both 14 pt.
+        // The line of the reply: 2 pt wide, 12 pt from the left, 8 pt from the top and 6 pt from the bottom of the header. The pictures
+        // are 8 pt from it.
+        let lineFrame = CGRect(x: 12.0, y: 8.0, width: 2.0, height: headerHeight - 8.0 - 6.0)
+        self.lineView.frame = lineFrame
+        self.lineView.tintColor = theme.chat.inputPanel.panelControlAccentColor
+        self.collageView.frame = CGRect(origin: CGPoint(x: lineFrame.maxX + 8.0, y: 9.0), size: CGSize(width: 40.0, height: 36.0))
+        let textX: CGFloat = self.collageView.frame.maxX + 8.0
+        self.titleLabel.frame = CGRect(x: textX, y: 9.0, width: max(0.0, cardWidth - textX - 44.0), height: 18.0)
+        self.subtitleLabel.frame = CGRect(x: textX, y: 28.0, width: max(0.0, cardWidth - textX - 44.0), height: 17.0)
+        self.chevronView.image = generateImage(CGSize(width: 16.0, height: 10.0), rotatedContext: { size, context in
+            context.clear(CGRect(origin: CGPoint(), size: size))
+            context.setStrokeColor(theme.chat.inputPanel.inputPlaceholderColor.cgColor)
+            context.setLineWidth(2.0)
+            context.setLineCap(.round)
+            context.setLineJoin(.round)
+            context.move(to: CGPoint(x: 2.0, y: size.height - 2.0))
+            context.addLine(to: CGPoint(x: size.width * 0.5, y: 2.0))
+            context.addLine(to: CGPoint(x: size.width - 2.0, y: size.height - 2.0))
+            context.strokePath()
+        })
+        // Where the close button of the reply is: 44 by 44 at the right edge.
+        self.chevronView.frame = CGRect(x: cardWidth - 44.0 + 10.0, y: floor((headerHeight - 24.0) * 0.5), width: 24.0, height: 24.0)
+        self.headerButton.frame = CGRect(x: cardFrame.minX, y: 0.0, width: cardWidth, height: headerHeight)
+        
+        let textFrame = CGRect(x: 12.0, y: headerHeight + 5.0, width: textWidth, height: textHeight)
+        self.textView.frame = textFrame
+        self.placeholderLabel.frame = CGRect(x: textFrame.minX, y: textFrame.minY + UIScreenPixel, width: textWidth, height: 20.0)
+        
+        let applyFrame = CGRect(origin: CGPoint(x: cardWidth - 3.0 - applySize.width, y: cardHeight - 3.0 - applySize.height), size: applySize)
+        self.applyBackground.frame = applyFrame
+        self.applyBackground.backgroundColor = theme.chat.inputPanel.panelControlAccentColor
+        self.applyBackground.layer.cornerRadius = applySize.height * 0.5
+        let _ = self.emojiView.update(
+            transition: .immediate,
+            component: AnyComponent(LottieComponent(
+                content: LottieComponent.AppBundleContent(name: "input_anim_smileToKey"),
+                color: theme.chat.inputPanel.inputControlColor,
+                startingPosition: .begin,
+                loop: false,
+                lottieSettings: self.context?.lottieRenderingSettings ?? .noAccountFallback
+            )),
+            environment: {},
+            containerSize: emojiSize
+        )
+        self.emojiView.frame = CGRect(origin: CGPoint(x: applyFrame.minX - 4.0 - emojiSize.width, y: headerHeight + rowHeight - minimalRowHeight + floor((minimalRowHeight - emojiSize.height) * 0.5)), size: emojiSize)
+        self.applyIcon.image = UIImage(bundleImageName: "Navigation/Done")?.withRenderingMode(.alwaysTemplate)
+        self.applyIcon.tintColor = theme.chat.inputPanel.actionControlForegroundColor
+        self.applyIcon.frame = CGRect(origin: CGPoint(), size: applyFrame.size)
+        self.applyButton.frame = applyFrame.offsetBy(dx: cardFrame.minX, dy: 0.0)
+        
+        // The button that throws the changes away, at the bottom of the card's left.
+        let closeFrame = CGRect(x: leftInset + sideInset, y: cardHeight - buttonSize, width: buttonSize, height: buttonSize)
+        transition.updateFrame(view: self.closeBackground, frame: closeFrame)
+        self.closeBackground.update(size: closeFrame.size, cornerRadius: buttonSize * 0.5, isDark: isDark, tintColor: .init(kind: .panel), isInteractive: true, transition: ComponentTransition(transition))
+        self.closeIcon.image = UIImage(bundleImageName: "Navigation/Close")?.withRenderingMode(.alwaysTemplate)
+        self.closeIcon.tintColor = theme.chat.inputPanel.panelControlColor
+        // The picture is 30 pt as it is made, and is shown 28 pt, in the middle of the button.
+        self.closeIcon.contentMode = .scaleAspectFit
+        let closeIconSide: CGFloat = 28.0
+        self.closeIcon.frame = CGRect(x: floor((closeFrame.width - closeIconSide) * 0.5), y: floor((closeFrame.height - closeIconSide) * 0.5), width: closeIconSide, height: closeIconSide)
+        self.closeButton.frame = closeFrame
+        
+        return cardHeight
+    }
+    
+    override func minimalHeight(interfaceState: ChatPresentationInterfaceState, metrics: LayoutMetrics) -> CGFloat {
+        return 92.0
+    }
+    
+    override func defaultHeight(metrics: LayoutMetrics) -> CGFloat {
+        return 92.0
+    }
+    
+    override func hitTest(_ point: CGPoint, with event: UIEvent?) -> UIView? {
+        let result = super.hitTest(point, with: event)
+        if result === self.view {
+            return nil
+        }
+        return result
+    }
+}
diff --git a/submodules/TelegramUI/Sources/AlbumEditSession.swift b/submodules/TelegramUI/Sources/AlbumEditSession.swift
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..dde3c46c19
--- /dev/null
+++ b/submodules/TelegramUI/Sources/AlbumEditSession.swift
@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@
+import Foundation
+import UIKit
+import TelegramCore
+import MediaPickerUI
+
+/// The edit of an album: what it was and what has been changed in the window that edits it. The window can be folded away; the session then
+/// waits in the place of the input panel (`AlbumEditInputPanelNode`) until the changes are saved or thrown away.
+final class AlbumEditSession {
+    /// The messages of the album that have a photo, in the order of the album.
+    let messages: [EngineRawMessage]
+    /// The pictures of the album as they were, in order, and every picture that has been given to the window (the added ones too).
+    var originalIdentifiers: [String]
+    var mediaById: [String: MediaPickerScreenImpl.Subject.Media]
+    /// Which message of the album (its place in the album) each picture is of.
+    var messageIndexByIdentifier: [String: Int] = [:]
+    /// The file of the picture of each message of the album (by its place), as it is on the phone.
+    var imageFiles: [Int: String] = [:]
+    /// The pictures that were added in high quality: they are scaled to a larger side when they are saved.
+    var highQualityIdentifiers: Set<String> = []
+    /// The pictures in the order they are in now.
+    var order: [String]
+    
+    let originalCaption: String
+    var caption: NSAttributedString
+    let originalIsCaptionAbove: Bool
+    var isCaptionAbove: Bool
+    var audio: (title: String, subtitle: String)?
+    
+    /// Whether the session waits in the place of the input panel.
+    var isBarVisible = false
+    /// The changes are being saved or thrown away: the folding away of the window is not to bring the panel back.
+    var isFinishing = false
+    
+    var changed: (() -> Void)?
+    var openRequested: (() -> Void)?
+    var applyRequested: (() -> Void)?
+    var discardRequested: (() -> Void)?
+    
+    init(messages: [EngineRawMessage], media: [MediaPickerScreenImpl.Subject.Media], caption: NSAttributedString, isCaptionAbove: Bool) {
+        self.messages = messages
+        var mediaById: [String: MediaPickerScreenImpl.Subject.Media] = [:]
+        var identifiers: [String] = []
+        for item in media {
+            let identifier = item.albumEditIdentifier
+            identifiers.append(identifier)
+            mediaById[identifier] = item
+        }
+        self.originalIdentifiers = identifiers
+        self.mediaById = mediaById
+        self.order = identifiers
+        self.originalCaption = caption.string
+        self.caption = caption
+        self.originalIsCaptionAbove = isCaptionAbove
+        self.isCaptionAbove = isCaptionAbove
+    }
+    
+    /// The pictures are taken as the window has them when it is opened for the first time, so that only what the user changes counts.
+    func setBaseline(_ identifiers: [String]) {
+        if !self.hasBaseline && !identifiers.isEmpty {
+            self.hasBaseline = true
+            self.originalIdentifiers = identifiers
+            self.order = identifiers
+        }
+    }
+    private var hasBaseline = false
+    
+    /// How many changes there are: every place where another picture is than there was, every added picture, the text, its place and the
+    /// audio file. Moving one picture to the place of another is two changes.
+    var changeCount: Int {
+        var count = 0
+        let original = Set(self.originalIdentifiers)
+        for index in 0 ..< min(self.order.count, self.originalIdentifiers.count) {
+            if self.order[index] != self.originalIdentifiers[index] {
+                count += 1
+            }
+        }
+        for identifier in self.order where !original.contains(identifier) {
+            count += 1
+        }
+        if self.caption.string != self.originalCaption {
+            count += 1
+        }
+        if self.isCaptionAbove != self.originalIsCaptionAbove {
+            count += 1
+        }
+        if self.audio != nil {
+            count += 1
+        }
+        return count
+    }
+    
+    /// The first three pictures of the album, for the small collage.
+    var collageImages: [UIImage] {
+        var result: [UIImage] = []
+        for identifier in self.originalIdentifiers.prefix(3) {
+            if let media = self.mediaById[identifier], case let .image(image) = media {
+                result.append(image)
+            }
+        }
+        return result
+    }
+}
diff --git a/submodules/TelegramUI/Sources/ChatAlbumPhotoContextMenu.swift b/submodules/TelegramUI/Sources/ChatAlbumPhotoContextMenu.swift
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..cf34c477ba
--- /dev/null
+++ b/submodules/TelegramUI/Sources/ChatAlbumPhotoContextMenu.swift
@@ -0,0 +1,1490 @@
+import Foundation
+import UIKit
+import UIKit.UIGestureRecognizerSubclass
+import LegacyComponents
+import LegacyMediaPickerUI
+import MediaPickerUI
+import MediaPasteboardUI
+import AttachmentUI
+import Photos
+import TelegramStringFormatting
+import Postbox
+import TextFormat
+import TelegramCore
+import Display
+import SwiftSignalKit
+import AccountContext
+import ContextUI
+import AppBundle
+import PresentationDataUtils
+import ImageCompression
+import TelegramPresentationData
+import UndoUI
+import ChatPresentationInterfaceState
+import ChatControllerInteraction
+import ChatMessageItemCommon
+import ChatMessageBubbleItemNode
+
+/// Whether a press on `message` is a press on one photo of an album: the message is one of several that make up the album, and it holds a
+/// photo. Such a press gets the menu of that photo alone (see `albumPhotoContextMenuItems`), not the menu of the whole album.
+func isAlbumPhotoMessage(_ message: EngineRawMessage, in messages: [EngineRawMessage]) -> Bool {
+    if messages.count < 2 || message.groupingKey == nil {
+        return false
+    }
+    return message.effectiveMedia.contains(where: { $0 is TelegramMediaImage })
+}
+
+private func renamedContextMenuAction(_ item: ContextMenuActionItem, text: String) -> ContextMenuActionItem {
+    return ContextMenuActionItem(
+        id: item.id,
+        text: text,
+        textColor: item.textColor,
+        textLayout: item.textLayout,
+        textFont: item.textFont,
+        icon: item.icon,
+        iconSource: item.iconSource,
+        iconPosition: item.iconPosition,
+        action: item.action
+    )
+}
+
+/// The menu of one photo of an album: Reply, Save to Photos, Forward, Delete, Select, Album Actions. Every item acts on this
+/// photo only. The items that need the rules of the regular message menu (who can reply, forward or delete, copy protection) are taken
+/// from the regular menu of this one message, so those rules stay in one place; the rest is added or renamed here.
+func albumPhotoContextMenuItems(
+    chatPresentationInterfaceState: ChatPresentationInterfaceState,
+    context: AccountContext,
+    message: EngineRawMessage,
+    controllerInteraction: ChatControllerInteraction?,
+    interfaceInteraction: ChatPanelInterfaceInteraction?,
+    photoIndex: Int,
+    photoCount: Int,
+    albumMessages: [EngineRawMessage],
+    showsAlbumActions: Bool,
+    albumReactions: AlbumReactionsBox? = nil,
+    albumActionsToggled: ((Bool) -> Void)?,
+    editPhoto: ((EngineMessage.Id) -> Void)?,
+    editAlbum: (() -> Void)?
+) -> Signal<ContextController.Items, NoError> {
+    let strings = chatPresentationInterfaceState.strings
+    let regularMenu = contextMenuForChatPresentationInterfaceState(
+        chatPresentationInterfaceState: chatPresentationInterfaceState,
+        context: context,
+        messages: [message],
+        controllerInteraction: controllerInteraction,
+        selectAll: false,
+        interfaceInteraction: interfaceInteraction,
+        messageNode: nil
+    )
+    return combineLatest(
+        regularMenu,
+        context.engine.data.get(TelegramEngine.EngineData.Item.Configuration.Limits())
+    )
+    |> map { items, limits -> ContextController.Items in
+        guard case let .list(regularItems) = items.content else {
+            return items
+        }
+
+        var reply: ContextMenuItem?
+        var forward: ContextMenuItem?
+        var delete: ContextMenuItem?
+        var select: ContextMenuItem?
+        for item in regularItems {
+            switch item {
+            case let .action(action):
+                if action.text == strings.Conversation_ContextMenuReply {
+                    reply = item
+                } else if action.text == strings.Conversation_ContextMenuForward {
+                    forward = item
+                } else if action.textColor == .destructive {
+                    delete = item
+                } else if action.text == strings.Conversation_ContextMenuSelect {
+                    select = item
+                }
+            case .custom:
+                // The delete item that shows a countdown of a message that disappears.
+                if delete == nil {
+                    delete = item
+                }
+            case .separator:
+                break
+            }
+        }
+
+        // Reply to the photo: the reply panel says which photo it is ("Reply to photo 4"), so the number is kept for it.
+        if case let .action(replyAction)? = reply {
+            let replyMessageId = message.id
+            reply = .action(ContextMenuActionItem(
+                id: replyAction.id,
+                text: replyAction.text,
+                textColor: replyAction.textColor,
+                textLayout: replyAction.textLayout,
+                textFont: replyAction.textFont,
+                icon: replyAction.icon,
+                iconSource: replyAction.iconSource,
+                iconPosition: replyAction.iconPosition,
+                action: { action in
+                    AlbumPhotoReplyStore.shared.setText(strings.Conversation_ContextMenuPhotoIndex("\(photoIndex + 1)", "\(photoCount)").string, for: replyMessageId)
+                    replyAction.action?(action)
+                }
+            ))
+        }
+
+        var result: [ContextMenuItem] = []
+        // Which photo of the album this is ("Photo 3 of 6"), small, like the line of the read time, with a line under it.
+        let noAction: ((ContextMenuActionItem.Action) -> Void)? = nil
+        result.append(.action(ContextMenuActionItem(text: strings.Conversation_ContextMenuPhotoIndex("\(photoIndex + 1)", "\(photoCount)").string, textColor: .primary, textLayout: .singleLine, textFont: .small, icon: { _ in
+            return nil
+        }, action: noAction)))
+        result.append(.separator)
+        if let reply {
+            result.append(reply)
+        }
+        
+        // Edit Photo: the ordinary edit of the message of this photo.
+        if let editPhoto, canEditMessage(accountPeerId: context.account.peerId, limitsConfiguration: limits, message: message) {
+            let messageId = message.id
